  "final_answer": "**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` posted to `/api/recommend`, but the Python backend only serves this endpoint at `/api/colleges/recommend` (`python-backend/api/routes.py`, line 243). That mismatch is the 404. The other client callers (`collegeApi.ts` and `useCollegeListGenerator.ts`) already use the right path.\n\n**Second bug behind the 404:** `suggestions.ts` sent `{ student_id, answers }`. The backend's `RecommendRequest` requires a top-level `student_profile` field, so fixing only the path would have produced a 422 error.\n\n**Fix:** In both calls in `suggestions.ts` (`generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`), I made two changes:\n- The URL is now `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- The body is now `{ student_profile: { student_id, answers } }`, which matches what the backend reads.\n\nI didn't add a second backend route, so the backend still has exactly one recommendation endpoint.\n\nI ran `tests/check_recommend.py` and it passes. It only reads the source files as text, so I haven't tried a live request against the backend.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`",
